wide|large-side-to-side|ADJECTIVE|large from side to side|Measuring a large distance from one side to the other.|rộng|The wide doorway allowed the table to pass through easily.|Ô cửa rộng giúp chiếc bàn được đưa qua dễ dàng.|Wide, wider, widest; a metre wide. Width is the related noun.|0
bible|christian-scripture|NOUN|Christian sacred writings|The collection of sacred writings used in Christianity.|Kinh Thánh|The display included a Bible with handwritten notes in the margins.|Khu trưng bày có một cuốn Kinh Thánh với những ghi chú viết tay bên lề.|Usually capitalized Bible for the Christian scripture; the Bible for the collection, a Bible for a physical copy.|-
federation|union-of-organizations|NOUN|union of organizations|A group of organizations joined together for shared purposes while keeping some independence.|liên đoàn|Several cycling clubs formed a federation to organize regional races.|Một số câu lạc bộ xe đạp thành lập một liên đoàn để tổ chức các cuộc đua trong vùng.|Countable; a federation of clubs. Member bodies retain some separate organization.|-
federation|union-of-states|NOUN|union of partly self-governing states|A country made up of states or regions that share a central government while retaining some powers of their own.|liên bang|In the fictional federation, each state managed its own school system.|Trong liên bang hư cấu, mỗi bang quản lý hệ thống trường học riêng.|Countable; a federation of states. Not every international organization is a federation.|-
morals|principles-of-right-and-wrong|NOUN|principles of right and wrong|Beliefs about what behaviour is right or wrong.|các nguyên tắc đạo đức|The story asks how personal morals influence difficult choices.|Câu chuyện đặt câu hỏi về cách các nguyên tắc đạo đức cá nhân ảnh hưởng đến những lựa chọn khó khăn.|Plural noun: someone's morals. Distinguish from the moral of a story, its lesson.|-
quite|moderately|ADVERB|to a moderate degree|To a noticeable but not extreme degree, especially in British English.|khá|The new reading room is quite spacious, though the main hall is larger.|Phòng đọc mới khá rộng rãi, dù hội trường chính rộng hơn.|Before gradable adjectives or adverbs; the strength varies with context, intonation and variety of English.|0
quite|completely|ADVERB|completely|Completely or entirely, especially with a word describing a complete state.|hoàn toàn|Your guess was quite correct: the parcel contained the missing notebook.|Bạn đoán hoàn toàn đúng: gói bưu kiện chứa cuốn sổ bị thất lạc.|Quite right, quite certain; not quite means not completely. Do not assume every use of quite has the same strength.|1
